From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako: keep the earjack
 debug supply on

The downstream mako kernel enables a 3.0 V regulator named "earjack_debug",
which is PM8921 L6, at boot for the headset-jack debug UART. L6 has no
consumer in the device tree, so the regulator core switches it off at late
boot and the jack UART loses that supply.

Mark it always-on, as downstream does. Not tested on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako.dts
index 29e52ce56b42..de0f325b6184 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-lg-nexus4-mako.dts
@@ -229,6 +229,8 @@ pm8921_l5: l5 {
 		pm8921_l6: l6 {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <3000000>;
+			/* "earjack_debug" supply for the headset jack UART */
+			regulator-always-on;
 			bias-pull-down;
 		};
 
